WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.497
[MUSIC]

00:00:08.497 --> 00:00:12.170
The value of communication in
today's world is only increasing.

00:00:12.170 --> 00:00:15.890
The way we do it is changing,
be it virtual with webinars or

00:00:15.890 --> 00:00:19.650
on our cellphones, but
communication is absolutely critical.

00:00:19.650 --> 00:00:23.480
Things are moving faster, there's
more information we have to process,

00:00:23.480 --> 00:00:27.380
we are multitasking at
rates never seen before.

00:00:27.380 --> 00:00:31.389
The ability to communicate clearly,
confidently, and

00:00:31.389 --> 00:00:35.991
in a compelling way is absolutely
critical to business success.

00:00:35.991 --> 00:00:41.744
[MUSIC]

00:00:41.744 --> 00:00:45.273
When it comes to virtual communication,
especially if you're on video,

00:00:45.273 --> 00:00:47.890
there are some things you
can do to really help.

00:00:47.890 --> 00:00:50.560
First, make sure you've
got good technology.

00:00:50.560 --> 00:00:53.130
Make sure there's a microphone
that picks up your voice.

00:00:53.130 --> 00:00:56.560
Make sure you have a camera
that displays things well.

00:00:56.560 --> 00:01:00.830
Make sure that the environment
you're speaking in is ready for you.

00:01:00.830 --> 00:01:04.660
So that means, make sure there's
nothing distracting behind you.

00:01:04.660 --> 00:01:07.519
Make sure you have a lighting,
so that you look decent.

00:01:07.519 --> 00:01:13.098
[MUSIC]

00:01:13.098 --> 00:01:17.141
Most of the lighting we have in our
workstations is not flattering when you're

00:01:17.141 --> 00:01:17.760
on camera.

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:20.880
You want elevated lighting
that's shining on you.

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:23.430
And when it comes to
actually communicating to

00:01:23.430 --> 00:01:28.430
people on the other end of your video
conference, look directly at the camera.

00:01:28.430 --> 00:01:31.320
The camera is as if you're
looking in their eyes.

00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:33.665
Many of us when we interact online,

00:01:33.665 --> 00:01:37.894
we look down because our notes are here,
our keyboard's here.

00:01:37.894 --> 00:01:41.786
It's as if we're talking to somebody's
shoes if you were having a face-to-face

00:01:41.786 --> 00:01:42.530
interaction.

00:01:42.530 --> 00:01:46.160
So it's really critical when you're
online, is you look at the camera and

00:01:46.160 --> 00:01:47.940
you focus there.

00:01:47.940 --> 00:01:51.470
Now you might be asking, how do I
know what to say, I need my notes?

00:01:51.470 --> 00:01:53.820
Tape some notes behind your camera.

00:01:53.820 --> 00:01:57.590
I actually, in my set up at home,
I went to the hardware store.

00:01:57.590 --> 00:02:03.160
I spent $10 for an outdoor light that
a mechanic uses to look under the hood.

00:02:03.160 --> 00:02:05.610
I mount that light behind my camera.

00:02:05.610 --> 00:02:10.550
I have an old music stand and on that
music stand, I have propped up my notes.

00:02:10.550 --> 00:02:14.640
So I'm lit well and I can see my
notes while looking at the camera.

00:02:14.640 --> 00:02:19.026
It makes a world of difference in coming
across as somebody who's engaged and

00:02:19.026 --> 00:02:19.777
connected.

00:02:19.777 --> 00:02:25.348
[MUSIC]

00:02:25.348 --> 00:02:27.038
People need to be prepared for

00:02:27.038 --> 00:02:30.958
all different types of communication
situations, be it a meeting,

00:02:30.958 --> 00:02:35.685
be it a presentation, be it being
an audience member in a presentation.

00:02:35.685 --> 00:02:39.705
I encourage everybody to go
into any communication event,

00:02:39.705 --> 00:02:44.615
thinking about what are the key
questions I have that I want answers to?

00:02:44.615 --> 00:02:48.605
Second, what are the key points or
themes that I want to get across?

00:02:48.605 --> 00:02:53.410
And with those themes, come up with
some examples to support them, or

00:02:53.410 --> 00:02:56.430
to reinforce what you're
trying to get across.

00:02:56.430 --> 00:03:00.844
If you go into any communication situation
with those questions in mind and

00:03:00.844 --> 00:03:05.117
those themes in your back pocket,
you will be able to contribute more and

00:03:05.117 --> 00:03:08.293
ultimately, take away more
from those situations.

00:03:08.293 --> 00:03:16.801
[MUSIC]

